//! task: write
//! ask: Declare a wire-format header struct with a 32-bit magic, two bytes, a reserved 16-bit field and a length, all big-endian.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.2
//! explain: `@transitus` marks a type that crosses a wire. Byte order belongs to the *place*: a field `u32:maior` reads and writes as a plain `u32`, and the conversion is the field access. `:nativus` (the in-process order) is illegal in a `@transitus` type (EXS-E0321). Fields are packed, alignment 1, no padding ever inserted, so a `reserva` field is written out explicitly rather than implied.

@transitus
publica structura Capitulum {
    signum:    u32:maior
    versio:    u8
    genus:     u8
    reserva:   u16:maior
    longitudo: u32:maior
}
